 to visitors  now there are calls to loosen  restrictions  family and essential care partners with  strict infection  prevention control measures do not play  a major role in the transmission of  covet  into the hospital when diane guy of  belleville suffered a stroke her husband  called 9-1-1  she was rushed to hospital and underwent  surgery alone  i'm in there and i'm my my mind is just  gone  i'm just petrified and the doctors  talking to me and i had no idea what  they were saying or anything  the impact of strict no visitor policies  at hospitals across canada was felt not  only by the sick  in addition to caring for patients we  found ourselves also being  placeholders for their families at  toronto's humber river hospital  effective this month a move to safely  reintroduce family to the bedside  prior to this we had 24 7 open visiting  and so we're not quite there yet but we  are a step closer  but visitor policies vary from one  hospital to the next  one unit to another heather lisa is  hopeful to have her family at her side  for her next appointment i don't see a  reason why a fully vaccinated  family member wouldn't be able to  accompany me to you  to appointments at this stage karen  lieberman  global news toronto  a slice of history is up for auction in  england four decades after it was served  it may not be quite as fresh as it was  at the wedding of charles and diana in  1981 when there were 23 official wedding  cakes served but  this slice is considered precious a  member of the queen mother's household  kept it  preserving it in plastic wrap inside a  tin the slice is expected to fetch  somewhere between  four hundred and seven hundred dollars  when it's auctioned off next month  oh and the auction house says we advise  against eating it  just in case you need that advice  a woman's place is on the podium next  team canada keeps hauling in the medals  canada's most decorated summer olympian  penny alexiac could break another record  tonight  a podium finish in the 100-meter  freestyle final would make her the only  canadian with seven olympic medals  global news spoke to penny's mother and  sister today ahead of the big race  we're probably way more stressed than  she is or maybe it's just me that stress  well my mom is very suspicious so she  makes us all  come to the same spot now every day  because after her first race went well  they were all sitting in the same spot  my mom's insistent that we all  come to the same spot  alexiak is inspired by american swimmer  michael phelps the most decorated  olympian of all time  her family says she speaks to him on a  regular basis  and i think hearing from him that you  know you really don't need to feel like  the you know the weight of the world's  on you  you know as long as you're focused on  what you want to do  and you're comfortable and you're happy  with what you've done and you feel that  you've put all your  energy and effort into it to be the best  that you can be um  that's enough and i think he you know  hearing that from him  i think really took on a different  perspective for her and i think really  helped her  such good advice penny alexia is part of  team canada's strong start at the tokyo  games after six days of competition  canada has ten medals two gold three  silver and five bronze  putting us in 12th spot for total number  of medals  all 10 of those medals have been won by  female athletes  it is inspiration to younger athletes  setting their sights on future olympics  redmond shannon looks at why the women  are dominating the start of these games  kaylee filmer and hilary johnson's take  bronze  in the coxless pairs it means as of  thursday  team canada's medal tally is 10  10-0 for the women from swimming to  softball  lifting to diving it's all about the  women  this is just a huge celebration of women  in sport and  they are giving us so much to cheer for  and really to be proud of  one reason for this could be simple math  at recent summer games  far more canadian women qualified for  events than men  and that is being reflected in the medal  count with  female athletes outshining their male  teammates  another reason could be the schedule  many sports with a legacy of  female canadian success are in the first  week  there's no question that swimming and  rowing are just  powerful for us but also we've made some  breakthroughs with judo  and non-traditional women's sport angela  schneider won silver in the cox fours in  the  less equal days of 1984 but even then  she noticed why canadian women could  succeed  i was so shocked when i went there to  see the way  other women were treated we were  we were treated so well in our country  comparatively speaking  in the pool canadian women and sport is  an organization that works to  help girls stay with sports even in  canada girls are  three times more likely than boys to  quit sports in their teenage years  they lose confidence in their body image  they lose confidence in their  skills as they go through those teen  years  sport can be a place when we're aware of  that sort of thing okay let's design  to counteract those sorts of things  alison sandmar graves says the recent  controversy over the norwegian handball  team uniforms  was an example of why women can feel  uncomfortable  in sports success she says is making  more girls  feel welcome olympic medals are a happy  bonus  more than a final goal redmond shannon  global news  london and that is global national for  this thursday i'm donna friesen  tonight's your canada is this beautiful  field of sunflowers  and lorette manitoba matches my jacket  thanks for watching  neetu garcia will be at the anchor desk  tomorrow and i'll see you again  in august take care of yourselves  [Music]  bye-bye
 

